# Terms, per attention layer of the Qwen3.6-35B-A3B decode step at 4,088..4,216 keys, M4 Pro (10 attention layers of 40):
#   flash, one dispatch alone, probe at 4,096 keys and 64 segments (the rule's count): shipped 138.0 us; fold staged
#   with the values dealt by stride + next-tile fetch into registers + masked straight-line tile arithmetic 89.2 us
#   (-48.8 us); the same terms at 1,088 keys and 32 segments: 63.0 -> 44.2 us. Each change is bit-identical to the shipped
#   flash (the probe's self-check at 1,024 keys, the kernel gate's bands, the e2e gate's ids).
#   profile of the base at depth 4,088 (mac-dec4): attn_flash 148.7 us a layer (probe lone 138.0 here: 0.93), step 11.17 ms
#   (11.07..11.63).
#   saving: 10 layers x 48.8 us x (0.6..1.1 of the probe figure's reach in a chain) = -0.29..-0.54 ms of 11.17
#   (-0.45 at the 0.93 centre): 89.5 -> 93.3 tok/s, +4.2 % (+2.6..+4.8)
kind: ab
question: Does the redesigned decode flash (staged fold, next-tile fetch, masked tile arithmetic) cut the 35B decode
  step at 4,088 keys by the 0.3 ms or more the stop rule asks, and by how much against the probe's prediction?
term: decode tok/s @ 128 tokens (decode_tok_s of generate_metal --ignore-eos -n 128), depth 4,088 (the first 4,088 ids of
  the 4,400-id prompt the mac-dec4 sitting used), ctx 4,352, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B MLX 4-bit split file, Apple M4 Pro
  20-core, head vs base 088286a77
unit: %
predict: 2.6..4.8
rounds: 6
sd: 1.5 % mac-dec4 report 3 (ours at 4,088 keys sd 3.4 % across rounds on the user's laptop; a pair inside one round cancels the drift, halving taken [unverified])
condition: Base and head are built on the testbed from their own trees; one fresh process per arm and round, arm order
  rotated every round, --repeat 2 on one open and the second run read; uptime and the stream probe at the start and
  end; thermal nominal; the decoded ids equal across arms (the head is bit-identical to the base).
decide-in: The redesign stands: land it with the kernel gate and e2e results, and open the flash's next terms (the
  fold's second pass, the loop's remaining skeleton) against the byte floor of 35 us a layer.
decide-below: Below +2.6 % the probe's lone figure does not carry into the chain: read generate_metal --profile
  attn_flash ms at 4,088 keys for both binaries (base 1.487 ms) and the stream probe before any further flash work.
decide-above: Above +4.8 % the saving includes more than the flash dispatch (the partials traffic or the launch gaps):
  split with --profile before pricing the next lever on the 10 layers.
